    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d686">

                <pb facs="0718" n="614" xml:id="pg614"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.00B/45: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in El Salvador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >McCafferty</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">San Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-01-21T10:00:00-06:00">January 21,
                            1932—10 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 1 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>10. Referring to my telegram No. 9, January 20, 3 p.m., because of communistic
                    disturbances martial law has been declared in the six departments of Ahuachapán,
                    Santa Ana, Sonsonate, La Libertad, San Salvador and Chalatenango.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">McCafferty</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
